(6554339, 974374, 39184, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by PennyClick:</b></div><hr/><i> Congratulations, Robert. A great idea and great shot. You really turn up the heat for these team challenges.  It''s impressive that you can do that so reliably.  For me it''s much more of a hit or miss thing! Using a camera strap these days. :-) ? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>LOL, that is so funny that you should ask about the camera strap.  I thought of you and Bear while I was shooting this <u>without</u> a strap and I knew that if you saw me that I would be admonished by both of you.  I didn''t come close to dropping it, but a couple of times the tarpon went for the camera and almost got it.  They were as big as me and definitely could have swallowed the D700 and 28-70 lens together.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-09-28 17:00:27.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by PennyClick: Congratulations, Robert. A great idea and great shot. You really turn up the heat for these team challenges.  It''s impressive that you can do that so reliably.  For me it''s much more of a hit or miss thing! Using a camera strap these days. :-) ?   LOL, that is so funny that you should ask about the camera strap.  I thought of you and Bear while I was shooting this without a strap and I knew that if you saw me that I would be admonished by both of you.  I didn''t come close to dropping it, but a couple of times the tarpon went for the camera and almost got it.  They were as big as me and definitely could have swallowed the D700 and 28-70 lens together.', '2011-09-28 17:59:14.000000', '2011-09-28 18:00:27.000000', 0),
(6554382, 973486, 132251, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by sinistral_leo:</b></div><hr/><i> Very abrupt DOF. this was basic editing? Strange kind of halos around the people also. almost dioramic. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Ah ha! Now I see why there was the "abrupt DOF" and "dioramic" effect.</td>', 'Originally posted by sinistral_leo: Very abrupt DOF. this was basic editing? Strange kind of halos around the people also. almost dioramic.   Ah ha! Now I see why there was the "abrupt DOF" and "dioramic" effect.', '2011-09-28 19:30:25.000000', NULL, 0),
